              "source",
              "runtime"
            ]
          },
          {
            "feature": "keyboard navigation",
            "owner": "component",
            "mechanism": "The plot is a single tab stop; arrow keys move between data points and the tooltip follows focus. Donut and radial charts keep that single stop.",
            "evidenceRefs": [
              "source",
              "runtime"
            ]
          },
          {
            "feature": "draw-finished signal",
            "owner": "component",
            "mechanism": "[data-slot=chart-plot] carries data-chart-state: measuring until the container has a width (a skeleton reserves the final size), drawing while series animate, and ready once drawing finishes, immediately when animation is off or prefers-reduced-motion is set. Headless capture waits for data-chart-state=ready.",
            "evidenceRefs": [
              "source",
              "runtime"
            ]
          },
          {
            "feature": "colour and identity",
            "owner": "component",
            "mechanism": "Series take chart-1 to chart-5 in slot order; a sixth series is rejected. A legend names every series by default when there are two or more, so identity is never colour-only; tooltip and axis text use text tokens, never a series colour.",
            "evidenceRefs": [
              "source",
              "runtime"
            ]
          },
          {
            "feature": "empty data",
            "owner": "component",
            "mechanism": "No rows, or only zero or null values, render an explicit No data state and still reach ready.",
